*TRAFFIC ADVISORY: Road Closures Due to Hurricane Lowell on Sept. 8*

L=C4=AAHU=E2=80=98E =E2=80=93 =C2=A0The Kaua=CA=BBi Police Department is ad=
vising the public about road conditions in the aftermath of Hurricane Lowel=
l, which has caused island-wide road closures. Crews from Hawai=CA=BBi Depa=
rtment of Transportation and Department of Public Works are responding to r=
oad hazards from flooding, fallen trees, landslides, downed power lines, an=
d debris.

*_Road Closures:_*


  * K=C5=ABhi=C5=8D Highway/Route 56 (north of Hanalei Bridge to Hanalei Do=
lphin Restaurant)=20
  * K=C5=ABhi=C5=8D Highway/Route 56 (Waikoko to Lumahai Beach)=20
  * K=C5=ABhi=C5=8D Highway/Route 56 (Kahiliholo Road to Kalihiwai Bridge) =

  * K=C5=ABhi=C5=8D Highway/Route 56 in K=C4=ABlauea (Traffic being diverte=
d to Kolo Road)=20
  * Hoone Road in Po=CA=BBip=C5=AB is impassable due to debris.=20

*_Partial Road Closures:_*


  * Kaumuali=CA=BBi Highway/Route 50 (Alternating one-lane traffic west of =
Kaua=CA=BBi Humane Society)=20

M=C4=81luhia Road (Tunnel of Trees) is open in both directions.

Motorists are urged to stay off the roads and limit travel to essential nee=
ds only in order to allow crews to assess damage from Hurricane Lowell, cle=
ar debris, and restore power quickly. Do not drive through flooded roadways=
 or around barricades and stay away from downed power lines.

Officials remind the public to use 9-1-1 only for life-threatening or time-=
critical emergencies. Calls to 9-1-1 for weather updates or general road co=
nditions can significantly delay emergency response. To report non-emergenc=
y road hazards, contact KPD Dispatch (non-emergency) at 808-241-1711.

Road and closure conditions are available at 808-241-1725.

